    "content": "Interesting puzzle! However, when I started solving it, I ran into the following questions: \nI understand that [[Ai]] and [[Bj]] are given in the input. Are these student specific (i.e. a student at the start standing at i = 1 will always keep [[A1]], no matter where I move the student to), or as soon as I move a student to location i=5 will his Ai become A5?\n- If it is the first, then it seems i is currently used for two things in your statement (both \"student [[i]]\" as well as 'the student is standing at [[i]]'). \n- If it is the second, then if I have 1 student of Alice's class, and then three of Bob's class, and then 1 of Alice's class, is that final student standing at i=5 or i=2?",
